{"black_box_warning":{"current_value":"No current FDA/DailyMed label identified.","fda_source_urls":["https://open.fda.gov/apis/drug/label/","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=progabide&limit=1","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=Gabrene&limit=1","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-approvals-and-databases/drugsfda-database"],"proposed_value":"No current FDA/openFDA label identified.","rationale":"The substantive finding of no current FDA label is consistent with the FDA/openFDA no-label result supplied in the row bundle, but DailyMed is not permissible for boxed-warning verification. Use FDA/openFDA wording only.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect"},"blocking_questions":["If exact French authorization/revocation dates must be retained, provide or permit the specific ANSM/public French medicines-directory source URL; ANSM is named in the row but is not in the allowed source-domain list for this audit."],"fact_checks":[{"current_value":"progabide","field":"generic_name","proposed_value":"progabide","rationale":"PubMed RCT records and NLM MeSH/PubChem records identify the substance as progabide.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6403342/","https://meshb.nlm.nih.gov/record/ui?ui=C017985","https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/44115"]},{"current_value":"","field":"alternate_generic_names","proposed_value":"halogabide; SL 76002; SL-76002; SL-76.002","rationale":"Important aliases/development codes are missing. NLM MeSH lists SL 76002 as an entry term; PubChem lists Halogabide and related SL code variants.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing","supporting_sources":["https://meshb.nlm.nih.gov/record/ui?ui=C017985","https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/44115"]},{"current_value":"Gabrene","field":"trade_names","proposed_value":"Gabrene; Gabren","rationale":"Gabrene is verified. PubChem also lists Gabren as a synonym; if the CSV treats brand/trade synonyms broadly, add Gabren to prevent duplicate-row creation under that alias.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing","supporting_sources":["https://meshb.nlm.nih.gov/record/ui?ui=C017985","https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/44115"]},{"current_value":"","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"Gabrene; Gabren; halogabide; SL 76002; SL-76002; SL-76.002","rationale":"Search aliases should include trade names and development-code aliases seen in NLM MeSH/PubChem so the same drug is not missed or duplicated.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing","supporting_sources":["https://meshb.nlm.nih.gov/record/ui?ui=C017985","https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/44115"]},{"current_value":"No - formerly authorized in France; authorization revoked/withdrawn","field":"available_in_us","proposed_value":"No - not FDA-approved/currently marketed in the US; historical French authorization/revocation requires ANSM source verification if retained.","rationale":"No current FDA/openFDA label was identified, supporting non-US availability. The exact French authorization/revocation statement is plausible from the row bundle but lacks an allowed-domain source in this audit.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"missing_source","supporting_sources":["https://open.fda.gov/apis/drug/label/","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-approvals-and-databases/drugsfda-database"]},{"current_value":"Historical/non-U.S. oral formulation","field":"formulations_available","proposed_value":"Historical/non-U.S. oral formulation","rationale":"Clinical trial evidence describes oral capsule dosing of progabide/placebo; no current US label was found.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6383790/"]},{"current_value":"Not FDA-approved/currently marketed","field":"maximum_approved_daily_dose","proposed_value":"Not FDA-approved/currently marketed","rationale":"No current FDA/openFDA label was identified, so there is no FDA-approved maximum daily dose.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://open.fda.gov/apis/drug/label/","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-approvals-and-databases/drugsfda-database"]},{"current_value":"Not FDA-approved/currently marketed","field":"minimum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"Not FDA-approved/currently marketed","rationale":"No current FDA/openFDA label was identified, so there is no FDA-approved minimum effective dose.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://open.fda.gov/apis/drug/label/","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-approvals-and-databases/drugsfda-database"]},{"current_value":"Historical/non-U.S. dosing individualized","field":"typical_doses_per_day","proposed_value":"Historical/non-U.S. dosing varied by trial; no current FDA-approved dosing.","rationale":"The cited trials used historical regimens rather than current approved dosing. Martinez-Lage used divided daily dosing; Schmidt reported an average daily dose of 2100 mg in a small add-on trial.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6383790/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6382068/"]},{"current_value":"Not FDA-cleared; ANSM France authorization 19/04/1984, revoked 21/07/2014","field":"year_fda_cleared","proposed_value":"Not FDA-cleared/approved; retain the French authorization/revocation dates only with the cited ANSM/public medicines-directory source.","rationale":"The FDA portion is supported by no FDA/openFDA label. The exact French dates are not verifiable from the allowed source domains supplied for this audit.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"missing_source","supporting_sources":["https://open.fda.gov/apis/drug/label/","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-approvals-and-databases/drugsfda-database"]},{"current_value":"GABA analog/prodrug with agonist activity at GABA-A and GABA-B receptors, enhancing inhibitory GABAergic signaling.","field":"mechanism_of_action","proposed_value":"GABA analog/prodrug with GABA-receptor agonist activity, including GABA-A/GABA-B activity reported in pharmacology records, enhancing inhibitory GABAergic signaling.","rationale":"PubMed pharmacology evidence supports specific GABA receptor agonist activity; NCBI/PubChem records support analog/prodrug and GABA-A/GABA-B wording.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6121050/","https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/44115"]},{"current_value":"High","field":"mechanism_confidence","proposed_value":"High","rationale":"Mechanism is supported by direct receptor-binding pharmacology and NCBI/PubChem records.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6121050/","https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/44115"]},{"current_value":"NCBI PubChem pharmacology records","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"NCBI PubChem pharmacology records; PubMed Lloyd 1982 GABA receptor pharmacology study","rationale":"PubChem supports the summary, and PubMed PMID 6121050 is a stronger primary pharmacology source for receptor agonist activity.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6121050/","https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/44115"]},{"current_value":"NCBI/PubChem","field":"mechanism_source_tier","proposed_value":"NCBI/PubChem; PubMed","rationale":"The current tier is acceptable but incomplete if PMID 6121050 is added as a primary mechanism source.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6121050/","https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/44115"]},{"current_value":"Limited data; hepatic metabolism and interaction concerns reported","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"Limited data; hepatic-enzyme elevations and clinically relevant interaction concerns reported, including effects on phenytoin/carbamazepine metabolism and microsomal epoxide hydrolase inhibition.","rationale":"Peer-reviewed sources report elevated hepatic enzymes, symptomatic hepatic enzyme elevation in one case, phenytoin interaction, carbamazepine-metabolism effects, and microsomal epoxide hydrolase inhibition.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/3098923/","https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1029073/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/3191894/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8222491/"]},{"current_value":"Liver","field":"major_organ_for_metabolism","proposed_value":"Liver","rationale":"The hepatic-enzyme and hepatic-metabolism/interactions literature supports liver/hepatic handling as the relevant metabolism/toxicity organ category.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/3098923/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8222491/","https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/44115"]},{"current_value":"Limited data","field":"half_life_range","proposed_value":"Limited data","rationale":"No current FDA label with a standardized half-life range was identified. Non-label secondary records report pharmacokinetic values, but the row's limited-data wording is appropriately conservative.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://open.fda.gov/apis/drug/label/","https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/44115"]},{"current_value":"Historical/unspecified epilepsy; Focal; Generalized","field":"epilepsy_type","proposed_value":"Historical/unspecified epilepsy; Focal; Generalized","rationale":"RCT evidence includes partial/complex partial epilepsy and severe epilepsies including generalized and partial subgroups.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6383790/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6357772/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6403342/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK581153/"]},{"current_value":"Unknown/limited data","field":"qt_interval_effect","proposed_value":"Unknown/limited data","rationale":"No current FDA label or QT-specific evidence was identified. Martinez-Lage reports ECG monitoring without treatment-related ECG changes, but not a QT-specific assessment.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6383790/"]},{"current_value":"Evidence availability: no reliable FDA/RCT symptom percentages found (0% usable quantified current data located)","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"Evidence availability: limited historical RCT adverse-event counts exist, but no current FDA-label or harmonized placebo-adjusted symptom-percentage table was identified.","rationale":"The Martinez-Lage RCT reports adverse-event counts during treatment periods, so '0% usable quantified current data' is misleading if read as no RCT safety counts. However, these data are small historical crossover counts, not current FDA-label percentages.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6383790/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6403342/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/3098923/"]},{"current_value":"NCBI PubChem pharmacology records; FDA/DailyMed labeling; ANSM French medicines directory","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"NCBI/PubMed and NCBI PubChem pharmacology records; FDA/openFDA labeling; PubMed placebo-controlled trial reports; ANSM French medicines directory for French authorization facts only if an allowed source URL is retained.","rationale":"DailyMed should not be cited for FDA boxed-warning verification. The row also uses PubMed RCT evidence and should name it. Exact ANSM date facts remain source-limited under this audit's allowed-domain list.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://open.fda.gov/apis/drug/label/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6121050/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6383790/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6357772/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6403342/"]},{"current_value":"No current FDA/DailyMed label identified.","field":"fda_black_box_warning","proposed_value":"No current FDA/openFDA label identified.","rationale":"DailyMed wording violates the audit rule for boxed warnings. Use FDA/openFDA only.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://open.fda.gov/apis/drug/label/","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=progabide&limit=1","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=Gabrene&limit=1"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed search on 05-20-2026: no current label found for terms [progabide; Gabrene].","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA label API search on 05-20-2026: no current FDA label found for terms [progabide; Gabrene; Gabren; SL 76002].","rationale":"Source wording should use FDA/openFDA and include key aliases. DailyMed is not permissible for this field.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://open.fda.gov/apis/drug/label/","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=progabide&limit=1","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=Gabrene&limit=1"]},{"current_value":"Former French-authorized GABA-ergic anticonvulsant (Gabrene); ANSM authorization later revoked/withdrawn.","field":"status_or_notes","proposed_value":"Former French-authorized GABA-ergic anticonvulsant (Gabrene); ANSM authorization later revoked/withdrawn. Exact French authorization details require the ANSM/public medicines-directory source URL.","rationale":"GABA-ergic mechanism and Gabrene alias are supported. The French authorization/revocation statement needs the specific ANSM source, which is outside the allowed-domain list supplied for this audit.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"missing_source","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6121050/","https://meshb.nlm.nih.gov/record/ui?ui=C017985"]},{"current_value":"Not available in US","field":"filter_availability","proposed_value":"Not available in US","rationale":"No current FDA/openFDA label was identified.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://open.fda.gov/apis/drug/label/","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-approvals-and-databases/drugsfda-database"]},{"current_value":"Unknown/limited","field":"filter_enzyme_effect","proposed_value":"Unknown/limited","rationale":"The literature reports interaction concerns but does not support a clean inducer/inhibitor classification suitable for this filter.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/3191894/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8222491/"]},{"current_value":"Focal; Generalized; Historical/unspecified epilepsy","field":"filter_epilepsy_type","proposed_value":"Focal; Generalized; Historical/unspecified epilepsy","rationale":"Consistent with RCT populations including partial/focal and generalized/severe epilepsies.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6383790/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6403342/"]},{"current_value":"Historical/not marketed","field":"filter_formulation","proposed_value":"Historical/not marketed","rationale":"No current US label was found; historical clinical trial dosing supports historical formulation use.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://open.fda.gov/apis/drug/label/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6383790/"]},{"current_value":"GABA","field":"filter_mechanism","proposed_value":"GABA","rationale":"Directly supported by receptor pharmacology and NCBI/PubChem records.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6121050/","https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/44115"]},{"current_value":"Liver/hepatic","field":"filter_metabolism","proposed_value":"Liver/hepatic","rationale":"Supported by hepatic enzyme/interactions literature.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/3098923/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8222491/"]},{"current_value":"Unknown/limited","field":"filter_qt_effect","proposed_value":"Unknown/limited","rationale":"No QT-specific FDA label or trusted QT evidence was identified.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://open.fda.gov/apis/drug/label/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6383790/"]},{"current_value":"Unquantified/limited data","field":"filter_symptom_category","proposed_value":"Unquantified/limited data","rationale":"Historical RCT safety counts exist but are not a current FDA-label percentage table.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6383790/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6403342/"]}],"generic_name":"progabide","missing_rcts":[],"outcome_checks":[{"current_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo RR50 differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","field":"diff_50_responder_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo RR50 differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","rationale":"The retained crossover RCT records do not provide a standard arm-level active and placebo 50% responder rate allowing a drug-minus-placebo RR50 differential. Martinez-Lage reports individual reductions but not extractable arm rates; Dam reports no significant partial-seizure difference; Loiseau is a crossover report without extractable differential RR50 in the accessible evidence.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6383790/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6357772/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6403342/"]},{"current_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo MPC differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","field":"diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo MPC differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","rationale":"The cited crossover RCT evidence does not provide a standard active-arm median percent change and placebo-arm median percent change suitable for a maximum-dose drug-minus-placebo MPC differential.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6383790/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6357772/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6403342/"]},{"current_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo seizure-freedom patient-rate differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","field":"diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo seizure-freedom patient-rate differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","rationale":"The retained PubMed RCT records do not provide active and placebo seizure-freedom patient rates suitable for calculating a differential.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6383790/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6357772/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6403342/"]},{"current_value":"","field":"plot_diff_50_responder_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"","rationale":"Blank plotting field is consistent with NR/not-extractable RR50 differential.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"not_a